(a) the details of implementation of Khelo Bharat Niti, 2025 and the initiatives taken to promote indigenous martial arts, particularly Thang-Ta;
(b) whether Government has taken note that Thang-Ta, originating from Manipur, has expanded to over 30 States and Union Territories, with recognised State, National and International Federations, and has been included in the Khelo India School Games and universities;
(c) whether financial assistance is proposed for its training, infrastructure and competitions; and
(d) the measures envisaged to promote Thang-Ta globally and strengthen indigenous sports under Khelo Bharat Niti, 2025, in line with India's Vision 2047?

(a) whether Government has utilised or proposes to utilise Nirbhaya Fund for ensuring safety, security and rehabilitation of women and girl Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) residing in relief camps in Manipur;
(b) whether any proposal has been received from GoM for establishing or strengthening One Stop Centres, Women Helplines, safe spaces, psychosocial counselling, legal aid and other gender-responsive support services in relief camps, and if so, details thereof;
(c) whether any special livelihood and economic rehabilitation programmes have been approved for displaced women, particularly widows, single women and female-headed households; and
(d) measures taken to ensure their long-term protection, dignity and socio-economic rehabilitation until normalcy is fully restored in the State?

(a) the current progress of implementing the AgriStack and Digital Agriculture Mission (DAM) to provide seamless advisory services nationwide including Manipur;
(b) the total number of farmers in Manipur and across the country successfully registered and issued unique digital identification numbers under farmers' Registry and Crop Sown Registry;
(c) whether Government has completely integrated this registry with State land records to expedite credit disbursements, improve access to crop insurance and weather advisories;
(d) if so, the details of cybersecurity protocols established to protect sensitive agricultural and personal data of rural farmers; and
(e) steps taken to utilize artificial intelligence for precision crop yield estimations?

(a) the number of first-time employees and employers in Manipur, received benefits/incentives under PMVBRY since its launch, district-wise and category-wise;
(b) the details of special provisions made to promote employment generation for IDPs in the State;
(c) whether Government has received any proposal from GoM, seeking special assistance under PMVBRY or any other employment generation scheme for rehabilitation and livelihood restoration of IDPs and if so, the details thereof and action taken thereon; and
(d) the steps taken to facilitate employment, skill-development and social security coverage for displaced youth and affected communities in Manipur, Employment Linked Incentive (ELI) Scheme and or Central employment initiatives?
